<!--
    The themed tile: the same three ruled lines, two ticked and one open, drawn
    as one silhouette. It is the foreground's drawing at the same coordinates —
    the two layers used to disagree, the foreground carrying a sheet the
    monochrome never had, which is half of why the sheet read as a square (#73).
    Strokes are a shade heavier, because a tint has no second colour to separate
    the ticks from the rules.
-->
